{"type":"data","nodes":[null,{"type":"data","data":[{"id":1,"title":2,"inWords":3,"equation":4,"parameters":5,"outputs":12,"results":14,"assumptions":17,"buildsOn":20,"sameDomain":21,"citation":37,"learnMore":38},"newton-second-law","Force, masse et accélération","Deuxième loi de Newton : la force (F) égale la masse (m) fois l'accélération (a). La même poussée accélère une masse plus légère davantage — c'est la loi sur laquelle s'appuient tous les autres échelons ici.","\u003Cspan class=\"katex-display\">\u003Cspan class=\"katex\">\u003Cspan class=\"katex-mathml\">\u003Cmath xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\">\u003Csemantics>\u003Cmrow>\u003Cmi>F\u003C/mi>\u003Cmo>=\u003C/mo>\u003Cmi>m\u003C/mi>\u003Cmi>a\u003C/mi>\u003C/mrow>\u003Cannotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">F = ma\u003C/annotation>\u003C/semantics>\u003C/math>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003Cspan class=\"katex-base\">\u003Cspan class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\">\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\">\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"mrel\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\">\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"katex-base\">\u003Cspan class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\">\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"mord mathnormal\">ma\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/span>",[6,9],{"label":7,"value":8},"Force [N]","100 (0 – 1 000 000 000)",{"label":10,"value":11},"Masse [kg]","100 (0,001 – 1 000 000 000)",[13],"Accélération",[15],{"label":13,"value":16},"1 m/s2",[18,19],"Masse ponctuelle","Pas de friction",[],[22,25,28,31,34],{"id":23,"title":24},"weight","Poids",{"id":26,"title":27},"free-fall","Chute libre",{"id":29,"title":30},"momentum","Quantité de mouvement",{"id":32,"title":33},"projectile","Portée d'un projectile",{"id":35,"title":36},"twr